{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\\n\\nusing namespace std;\\n\\nint A[1000][1000];\\n\\ntypedef long long ll;\\n\\nll solve(int m, int n, int k) {\\n  const int paired = min(m, n);\\n  const int scanned = max(m, n);\\n  vector<int> transposed;\\n  vector<const int *> rows(paired);\\n\\n  if (m <= n) {\\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i)\\n      rows[i] = A[i];\\n  } else {\\n    transposed.resize(static_cast<size_t>(m) * n);\\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i)\\n      for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\\n        transposed[static_cast<size_t>(j) * m + i] = A[i][j];\\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\\n      rows[j] = transposed.data() + static_cast<size_t>(j) * m;\\n  }\\n\\n  vector<int> band(scanned);\\n  unordered_map<ll, ll> h;\\n  ll ans = 0;\\n  for (int first = 0; first < paired; ++first) {\\n    fill(band.begin(), band.end(), 0);\\n    for (int last = first; last < paired; ++last) {\\n      const int *row = rows[last];\\n      int *sums = band.data();\\n      // Distinct positions have no dependencies in this update.\\n#pragma GCC ivdep\\n      for (int pos = 0; pos < scanned; ++pos)\\n        sums[pos] += row[pos];\\n\\n      // Prefix frequencies must be queried and updated in scan order.\\n      h.clear();\\n      h[0] = 1;\\n      ll s = 0;\\n      for (int pos = 0; pos < scanned; ++pos) {\\n        s += sums[pos];\\n        ans += h.find(s - k) != h.end() ? h[s - k] : 0;\\n        h[s]++;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return ans;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n  int k, m, n;\\n  cin >> k >> m >> n;\\n  memset(A, 0, sizeof A);\\n\\n  for (int i = 0; i < m; i++)\\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)\\n      cin >> A[i][j];\\n\\n  cout << solve(m, n, k) << endl;\\n  return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/main.cpp\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"Pairing boundaries along the smaller dimension and separating contiguous, SIMD-safe band updates from the dependent frequency scan should reduce work and memory stalls.\",\"notes\":\"The hash strategy and I/O remain unchanged. Band sums fit int under the stated limits; prefix sums and counts remain 64-bit. Work buffers are local and reset between bands. No commands or measurements were performed.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Pair over min(m,n), reducing complexity to O(min(m,n)^2*max(m,n)).\",\"Reuse contiguous input rows when m<=n; otherwise transpose once to make each added slice contiguous.\",\"Replace strided prefix accesses with incremental band sums, applying GCC ivdep only to the independent elementwise additions. Preserve the sequential prefix-frequency dependency, including for k=0.\"]}"}}
